WEBVTT

00:17.540 --> 00:19.580
(Byeon Woo Seok)

00:21.150 --> 00:22.348
(CEO)

00:22.349 --> 00:23.349
(10 missed calls from CEO)

00:25.949 --> 00:27.919
(Kim Hye Yoon)

00:34.660 --> 00:37.999
(Lovely Runner)

00:42.100 --> 00:43.459
(July 22, 2009)

00:43.860 --> 00:44.869
Are we rolling right now?

00:47.369 --> 00:48.769
- Gosh. Look at that.
- Over there!

00:48.770 --> 00:49.839
- There it is!
- Gosh.

00:52.069 --> 00:53.139
Hey, what's that?

00:53.910 --> 00:54.940
- Look at that.
- What?

00:55.009 --> 00:56.139
- What is that?
- Look!

00:56.709 --> 00:58.410
- This is so fascinating!
- Oh, my. So beautiful.

00:58.749 --> 00:59.810
- I mean, how...
- Gosh.

01:07.850 --> 01:09.819
Did you all take a look at the sky just now?

01:09.959 --> 01:11.788
There hasn't been a total solar eclipse...

01:11.789 --> 01:13.060
of this magnitude in the past 61 years.

01:13.329 --> 01:15.559
The Moon is smaller than the Sun by 400 times.

01:15.560 --> 01:16.729
- When I saw the Moon slowly...
- Are you ready?

01:16.730 --> 01:18.569
- swallowing up the Sun gradually...
- Okay. Great.

01:18.800 --> 01:19.800
- Get in.
- It felt...

01:19.801 --> 01:21.099
- so surreal to watch it.
- How can you smile right now?

01:21.100 --> 01:22.799
- It gave me a feeling that...
- Let's go.

01:22.800 --> 01:24.339
something incredible would happen.

01:24.640 --> 01:28.240
I was sort of wishful that a miracle would happen to me.

01:28.410 --> 01:30.079
- So I hope that...
- I'll get going now.

01:30.080 --> 01:32.280
your lives will be blessed with a miracle.

01:32.580 --> 01:34.949
We will begin Part One of the show after this song.

01:38.119 --> 01:39.520
Hey, we're late. Hurry up.

01:39.690 --> 01:40.690
Let's go.

01:41.020 --> 01:42.159
Hello.

01:42.160 --> 01:43.819
- Hello. We're Eclipse.
- Hello. We're Eclipse.

01:45.990 --> 01:48.089
Hello.

01:48.259 --> 01:49.660
Hello, we're Eclipse.

01:49.860 --> 01:51.600
- Hello!
- Hello!

01:52.929 --> 01:54.130
Then there's no break.

02:01.509 --> 02:02.539
No way.

02:03.410 --> 02:04.979
Okay. I can rest up after this then.

02:05.350 --> 02:06.410
Yu Ri.

02:06.580 --> 02:08.179
I'm a huge fan of yours.

02:08.750 --> 02:10.080
Can I tell you my wish?

02:10.419 --> 02:11.750
Sir, you can't do this here.

02:12.149 --> 02:13.149
It's fine.

02:13.150 --> 02:14.190
He's my fan.

02:15.160 --> 02:16.319
What's your wish?

02:24.100 --> 02:25.699
- Please hurry.
- Okay.

02:26.870 --> 02:28.370
- Let's begin right away.
- Hello.

02:28.870 --> 02:30.299
- Don't mess it up. Okay?
- Okay.

02:30.440 --> 02:31.739
Do a good job. Okay?

02:32.069 --> 02:33.069
One, two, three.

02:33.070 --> 02:34.469
- Hello, we're Eclipse.
- Hello, we're Eclipse.

02:34.470 --> 02:35.509
- We can't wait to work with you!
- We can't wait to work with you!

02:38.579 --> 02:40.849
All right, we've had the opportunity...

02:40.850 --> 02:43.880
to hear a nice introduction for each member of Eclipse.

02:44.280 --> 02:45.689
By the way, there's something...

02:45.690 --> 02:47.288
all the new singers on our show must go through.

02:47.289 --> 02:49.518
- I should paint your toenails...
- It's to test...

02:49.519 --> 02:52.190
- your popularity with the public.
- with your favorite color, yellow.

02:52.359 --> 02:55.229
- Yellow.
- Yes!

02:55.259 --> 02:56.698
It's a great way to gauge...

02:56.699 --> 02:58.728
- the public's reception...
- Sol.

02:58.729 --> 02:59.829
- of your song.
- Look out the window.

03:00.069 --> 03:02.970
It's so sunny today. The weather is amazing.

03:03.039 --> 03:04.239
Should we go out for a walk?

03:04.669 --> 03:07.609
The doctor said lying in bed all day wouldn't do you any good.

03:08.380 --> 03:09.879
To practice navigating in the wheelchair,

03:09.880 --> 03:12.549
- I'll go first.
- let's try moving around a bit.

03:13.180 --> 03:14.909
- Yes?
- Hello.

03:14.910 --> 03:17.549
I'm so busy. Who's calling me?

03:17.819 --> 03:18.850
Who is this?

03:19.650 --> 03:22.219
This is the leader of a new group, Eclipse. My name is Baek In Hyuk.

03:22.220 --> 03:23.919
What? Your name is Back In The Day?

03:25.289 --> 03:27.560
- She said, "Back In The Day." - Oh, no. You failed.

03:28.359 --> 03:29.599
- Oh, no.
- Hello.

03:29.600 --> 03:31.130
- Oh, no. Sol. This must hurt.
- We're calling...

03:31.329 --> 03:32.529
- from a live radio show.
- Are you okay?

03:32.530 --> 03:34.029
Eclipse is joining us today.

03:34.030 --> 03:35.869
- Sol.
- So we were running...

03:35.870 --> 03:37.269
a popularity test with our listeners.

03:38.039 --> 03:40.470
- Is that so?
- All right. Ma'am.

03:40.569 --> 03:42.880
Let me give you a special hint.

03:42.940 --> 03:44.538
It's a surprise guest that comes to us...

03:44.539 --> 03:46.108
during the hot summer out of the blue.

03:46.109 --> 03:48.180
- I'm sorry. I cut it too short.
- When you see this,

03:48.579 --> 03:50.018
you can also see the rainbow.

03:50.019 --> 03:51.549
I'll hurry and get some ointment.

03:51.650 --> 03:53.250
Guess what this is.

03:58.120 --> 03:59.489
I'm such a klutz. Seriously.

04:01.829 --> 04:04.900
- The answer was the sudden shower.
- Gosh, the sudden shower.

04:05.030 --> 04:08.568
Okay, ma'am. Thank you for answering our call.

04:08.569 --> 04:10.538
Unfortunately, you couldn't give us the correct answer.

04:10.539 --> 04:13.269
However, you know that we're quite generous right here...

04:13.340 --> 04:14.810
on "Hamster Seung Yeon's 10-10 Friend."

04:15.079 --> 04:17.880
Just like In Hyuk's brimming confidence,

04:17.910 --> 04:19.780
our show brims with generosity.

04:20.579 --> 04:23.219
We'll send you a present for accepting our call,

04:23.220 --> 04:24.479
ma'am.

04:24.519 --> 04:27.189
We'll send you a red ginseng gift set,

04:27.190 --> 04:30.160
so you could maintain good health for a long time.

04:30.660 --> 04:31.660
- Congratulations.
- Congratulations.

04:31.661 --> 04:32.759
- Congratulations.
- Congratulations.

04:33.329 --> 04:35.429
We'll continue with the second try.

04:35.559 --> 04:38.260
Who should try after In Hyuk?

04:38.570 --> 04:40.369
Why don't you give it a try, Sun Jae?

04:40.700 --> 04:42.070
Oh, sure.

04:44.999 --> 04:46.470
Your phone is ringing.

04:52.309 --> 04:54.609
No one is answering the phone.

04:55.220 --> 04:57.950
I hope you'll at least get to try even if you succeed in the end.

05:00.520 --> 05:02.220
That's so noisy.

05:02.660 --> 05:04.460
Just answer it.

05:23.640 --> 05:24.710
Hello?

05:26.309 --> 05:28.780
Can you hear my voice?

05:30.350 --> 05:32.590
- What's this?
- Hello. My name is...

05:33.289 --> 05:34.950
Ryu Sun Jae.

05:35.960 --> 05:37.020
So what?

05:37.260 --> 05:38.320
Do you know who I am?

05:39.129 --> 05:40.330
I don't.

05:42.799 --> 05:44.359
Do you know Eclipse?

05:44.400 --> 05:45.628
We made a debut two months ago.

05:45.629 --> 05:46.868
I said I didn't know who you were.

05:46.869 --> 05:49.368
That was another failed attempt. What a bummer.

05:49.369 --> 05:53.209
Okay. Hello. Thank you for accepting our call.

05:53.210 --> 05:56.178
This is DJ Hamster from "Hamster Seung Yeon's 10-10 Friend."

05:56.179 --> 05:57.439
I'm hanging up.

05:57.580 --> 06:00.080
Hold on. Don't forget about your present.

06:00.809 --> 06:02.118
- I'm good.
- The weather...

06:02.119 --> 06:03.418
has been amazing lately.

06:03.419 --> 06:05.248
We'll give you a pair of functional running shoes,

06:05.249 --> 06:08.219
so you can wear them when you go on a picnic.

06:08.220 --> 06:09.590
I don't need them.

06:11.689 --> 06:14.789
I wonder what kind of present you would like then.

06:14.960 --> 06:17.529
How about the latest indoor exercise bike?

06:17.530 --> 06:19.030
I said I didn't want anything.

06:19.330 --> 06:21.200
I don't need whatever you're trying to give me.

06:21.840 --> 06:22.939
You call that a present?

06:23.270 --> 06:25.339
Do you think you can make me walk again?

06:25.340 --> 06:26.869
That's what I want!

06:27.939 --> 06:29.339
If you can't even do that,

06:29.340 --> 06:30.678
why are you calling me and harassing me...

06:30.679 --> 06:31.809
when I haven't asked for this?

06:32.479 --> 06:34.179
Are you having fun, doing prank calls like this?

06:36.220 --> 06:37.779
Good for you guys...

06:37.780 --> 06:39.220
that life is fun for you.

06:41.720 --> 06:43.119
Somewhere in this world,

06:44.020 --> 06:45.989
there are people who don't want to live...

06:46.629 --> 06:49.059
because the weather is darn too good.

06:50.530 --> 06:52.668
So don't do prank calls like this ever again.

06:52.669 --> 06:54.830
You're making me want to set your TV station on fire!

06:59.439 --> 07:01.608
I see. I'm so sorry.

07:01.609 --> 07:03.108
It wasn't our intention...

07:03.109 --> 07:04.179
Wait.

07:05.549 --> 07:06.650
Are you still listening?

07:08.650 --> 07:09.780
You're listening, right?

07:12.450 --> 07:13.619
Mom.

07:13.789 --> 07:14.789
Mom! Turn this off.

07:14.790 --> 07:15.859
"Thank you..."

07:17.320 --> 07:18.520
"for staying alive."

07:21.489 --> 07:23.700
Your loved ones around you would be relieved...

07:24.900 --> 07:26.169
and be grateful...

07:26.970 --> 07:28.200
that you are still with them.

07:33.970 --> 07:35.239
So...

07:37.539 --> 07:38.650
you should live your life...

07:39.850 --> 07:40.950
today...

07:43.080 --> 07:44.520
because it's a great day.

07:45.820 --> 07:47.189
It will rain tomorrow.

07:47.350 --> 07:48.350
Then...

07:49.619 --> 07:51.520
as you wait until the rain stops,

07:53.689 --> 07:54.830
live another day.

07:56.059 --> 07:57.499
If you keep this up,

07:59.169 --> 08:01.729
there might come a day when life doesn't seem so miserable.

08:02.999 --> 08:04.069
Gosh. Come on.

08:04.070 --> 08:05.769
I would like to apologize sincerely...

08:05.770 --> 08:07.238
to the people who accepted our calls...

08:07.239 --> 08:09.609
- and our listeners.
- What is it?

08:10.879 --> 08:11.979
What's wrong?

08:12.379 --> 08:15.679
After we listen to "Sonaki" by Eclipse,

08:15.979 --> 08:19.619
we'll come back with Part Two of the show.

08:26.160 --> 08:27.830
Cry it out. It's okay.

08:32.270 --> 08:33.270
It's okay.

08:38.369 --> 08:39.640
It's okay.

08:52.649 --> 08:55.590
(December 31, 2022)

08:56.259 --> 08:57.259
(Ryu Sun Jae)

08:57.260 --> 08:58.729
(Episode 1)

09:02.830 --> 09:03.929
(Let's kidnap Sun Jae and run!)

09:03.930 --> 09:05.228
(Sun Jae)

09:05.229 --> 09:06.799
(Let's kidnap Sun Jae and run!)

09:06.800 --> 09:08.330
(I love you, Ryu Sun Jae.)

09:12.310 --> 09:13.739
(Resume)

09:31.060 --> 09:32.430
(Alarm)

09:37.300 --> 09:38.429
Come on.

09:38.430 --> 09:39.969
I submitted my resume a long time ago.

09:39.970 --> 09:42.070
If they were going to hire me, they would've already contacted me.

09:42.999 --> 09:45.869
I shouldn't expect anything from it. Let's just move on.

09:48.369 --> 09:49.540
You startled me!

09:52.710 --> 09:54.850
What's that on your face, Grandma?

09:56.779 --> 09:59.090
Miss, you look so pretty.

10:01.350 --> 10:02.519
Am I pretty?

10:03.889 --> 10:04.960
Yes.

10:14.899 --> 10:17.269
How did you get that out?

10:17.869 --> 10:19.369
Let me see your hand, Grandma.

10:21.970 --> 10:23.310
You wish!

10:25.710 --> 10:27.579
Where did she learn to talk like that?

10:27.580 --> 10:28.820
- Grandma!
- Whatever!

10:28.879 --> 10:31.320
Give it back! Come on, let me have it.

10:36.159 --> 10:37.419
Grandma!

10:37.420 --> 10:39.789
- Hello.
- Hello.

10:39.790 --> 10:41.589
- Mom.
- What is it this time?

10:41.590 --> 10:43.460
This old lady is scary!

10:43.600 --> 10:45.060
You called me Miss earlier!

10:45.430 --> 10:47.170
Come on. That's my dear Sun Jae's.

10:47.600 --> 10:49.268
I'm going to die if she makes a scratch on that!

10:49.269 --> 10:51.399
- No way.
- Please! Oh, no.

10:51.739 --> 10:53.169
Grandma, come on!

10:53.170 --> 10:55.008
Dear me!

10:55.009 --> 10:56.580
- I'm home.
- You're back.

10:57.080 --> 10:59.210
- Another all-nighter at work?
- Where are you going, Grandma?

10:59.550 --> 11:01.049
That jerk, General Manager Kim.

11:01.050 --> 11:03.080
I should just quit my job or something. Seriously.

11:03.279 --> 11:05.080
- Did you eat?
- I must go back after a shower.

11:05.550 --> 11:07.450
- Again?
- Grandma!

11:08.420 --> 11:11.119
Geum! Can you take that from her? Please?

11:11.420 --> 11:13.989
Gosh. She'll give it back to you once she's done playing with it.

11:14.330 --> 11:15.899
- Come on.
- Right.

11:16.930 --> 11:18.430
Oh, no!

11:18.899 --> 11:20.268
Mom!

11:20.269 --> 11:22.440
Okay. Just sit tight.

11:22.470 --> 11:24.570
- Mom.
- Oh, no.

11:24.800 --> 11:26.440
If you give it back to me,

11:26.470 --> 11:28.540
I'll let you watch "Secret Jouju."

11:29.479 --> 11:31.580
- Jouju?
- Yes.

11:31.979 --> 11:33.810
- Bibbidi boo.
- Bibbidi boo.

11:34.409 --> 11:35.819
My dear Mal Ja.

11:35.820 --> 11:37.819
- Are you in a good mood?
- Yes.

11:37.820 --> 11:39.888
Gosh. You brat. It's just a watch.

11:39.889 --> 11:41.550
Why are you yelling at your grandma at this hour?

11:42.590 --> 11:43.919
All right. Let's watch...

11:43.920 --> 11:45.289
- "Secret Jouju." - It's not "just" a watch.

11:45.290 --> 11:47.159
I bought this at an auction. I paid 3,000 dollars for this.

11:47.460 --> 11:48.489
Three thousand dollars?

11:49.029 --> 11:50.129
Three thousand dollars?

11:51.300 --> 11:53.128
It was 300 dollars.

11:53.129 --> 11:55.070
Goodness. That was a slip of the tongue.

11:55.570 --> 11:56.600
There's a power struggle going on...

11:56.700 --> 11:58.440
between my brain and my lips these days. Right.

11:58.769 --> 12:00.939
Seriously. You must be the most enthusiastic fan.

12:00.940 --> 12:03.209
Goodness. You sure are the most loyal fan.

12:03.210 --> 12:04.680
- Get my spell!
- Gosh.

12:04.909 --> 12:06.879
So the concert is today?

12:07.550 --> 12:08.550
Yes.

12:08.551 --> 12:10.649
It's been five years since their last concert.

12:21.389 --> 12:22.600
Hey, Sun Jae.

12:23.029 --> 12:24.100
What happened?

12:29.470 --> 12:32.210
You met with Director Park and said you wouldn't do the movie.

12:32.440 --> 12:33.509
Are you out of your mind?

12:38.009 --> 12:39.050
Sun Jae.

12:39.379 --> 12:40.909
Didn't I tell you?

12:41.109 --> 12:43.849
I said you could take a long break once you were done with this movie.

12:43.850 --> 12:45.080
I said I wanted to retire.

12:45.519 --> 12:46.749
I didn't ask for a break.

12:50.690 --> 12:51.989
Why don't you just go out there?

12:52.859 --> 12:54.858
Look at the sea of people out there. They're your fans who came...

12:54.859 --> 12:56.430
to watch you perform after waiting for years and on.

12:56.659 --> 12:58.560
You're going to regret this later!

12:58.600 --> 12:59.629
Regret?

13:01.970 --> 13:02.999
I won't regret it.

13:04.499 --> 13:06.269
Your body will remain,

13:06.670 --> 13:07.909
but your spirit will leave this world...

13:08.070 --> 13:10.009
when you have fulfilled the time in this world.

13:10.210 --> 13:12.809
Gosh, you can't ask me to edit this at the last minute like this.

13:12.810 --> 13:14.908
I have an important plan today. Seriously.

13:14.909 --> 13:16.720
Have you forgotten that I'm your first client?

13:16.920 --> 13:18.449
Then I'll hire someone else.

13:18.450 --> 13:20.889
Gosh. Come on, don't be like that.

13:21.519 --> 13:23.388
By the way, didn't Sanzu Bridge appear...

13:23.389 --> 13:24.920
in a drama or something?

13:26.060 --> 13:27.859
You must have enjoyed watching the drama.

13:27.960 --> 13:29.759
Gosh, don't tell me.

13:30.200 --> 13:31.629
Are you Jang Man Weol?

13:31.930 --> 13:33.469
The crew did a good job...

13:33.470 --> 13:34.499
at integrating authentic elements into the drama.

13:34.570 --> 13:35.999
You think only the living realm undergoes development?

13:36.170 --> 13:38.669
They build bridges over rivers in the afterlife too.

13:38.670 --> 13:39.809
Gosh, I got it.

13:39.810 --> 13:41.570
How would I know that? I haven't been to the afterlife.

13:42.409 --> 13:43.580
All done.

13:44.080 --> 13:45.310
(Grandma Celestial)

13:46.909 --> 13:48.249
I'll post it now.

13:51.950 --> 13:53.290
I'm late! Oh, no!

13:53.989 --> 13:55.149
Come on.

13:56.619 --> 13:57.619
(Let's kidnap Sun Jae and run!)

14:05.930 --> 14:07.700
I almost forgot the most important thing.

14:15.009 --> 14:16.210
(Eclipse's Concert)

14:21.810 --> 14:22.878
You.

14:22.879 --> 14:24.479
Will you keep putting me under your spell?

14:25.749 --> 14:28.249
I love you so much.

14:31.159 --> 14:32.190
See you soon.

14:32.659 --> 14:33.659
Bye.

14:37.060 --> 14:38.898
I've got zero problems

14:38.899 --> 14:42.200
I'll start running again right now

14:44.399 --> 14:45.969
- Are you that happy?
- Of course!

14:45.970 --> 14:46.970
It's my first time seeing him in person.

14:46.971 --> 14:48.009
Of course, I'm thrilled.

14:48.040 --> 14:49.479
Thank you. I know you're busy.

14:49.580 --> 14:50.879
Don't mention it.

14:50.979 --> 14:52.108
I switched to a big car...

14:52.109 --> 14:53.450
so I could give you a ride like this.

14:55.080 --> 14:56.579
Check the shopping bag there.

14:56.580 --> 14:57.720
It's a present from me.

14:58.119 --> 14:59.220
What is it?

15:01.790 --> 15:02.859
(Jagam High School)

15:03.389 --> 15:06.559
- Hey!
- Hey!

15:06.560 --> 15:08.028
It turned out my junior's older brother was...

15:08.029 --> 15:09.699
in Graduating Class 13 at Jagam High School.

15:09.700 --> 15:11.228
I asked to borrow it.

15:11.229 --> 15:14.330
Oh, my! I can't believe this!

15:14.629 --> 15:16.340
Was Sun Jae in Class Five when he was a senior?

15:16.800 --> 15:19.970
Class Five... Let's see.

15:22.440 --> 15:23.840
Oh, my.

15:23.940 --> 15:25.779
He's been so handsome even in high school.

15:25.850 --> 15:28.209
I totally want to kidnap him and run!

15:28.210 --> 15:29.618
Why didn't you do that when you had the chance?

15:29.619 --> 15:31.220
You could have done that if you wanted.

15:31.350 --> 15:33.118
Exactly. His school was across from ours.

15:33.119 --> 15:34.389
How come we never saw him?

15:34.790 --> 15:37.820
How did we miss such a dazzling young man back then?

15:38.190 --> 15:39.258
Had I been his fan since high school,

15:39.259 --> 15:40.528
I would've been the most successful fan.

15:40.529 --> 15:43.800
That's because you were someone else's fan back then.

15:44.629 --> 15:45.629
Like who?

15:47.869 --> 15:50.470
Right. I was.

15:51.269 --> 15:52.509
Which class was he in?

15:52.710 --> 15:53.840
He's not in the yearbook.

15:54.369 --> 15:55.710
Was it after your accident?

15:56.609 --> 15:58.638
Was he in a group fight with students from the adjacent school?

15:58.639 --> 16:00.680
Anyway, it was a huge scandal.

16:01.050 --> 16:02.050
He could've gotten expelled,

16:02.051 --> 16:03.749
but they just let him withdraw from school.

16:03.850 --> 16:04.950
I didn't know.

16:08.320 --> 16:09.519
- Hyun Ju.
- Yes.

16:09.920 --> 16:11.220
Can I cut out Sun Jae's picture?

16:11.320 --> 16:12.988
Sure. It's not mine. Do whatever you want.

16:12.989 --> 16:14.629
Thank your junior's brother for me.

16:20.930 --> 16:21.930
One, two, three.

16:25.499 --> 16:26.509
(Sun Jae over stars.)

16:27.540 --> 16:28.540
This is cute.

16:28.541 --> 16:29.809
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

16:29.810 --> 16:30.810
(We're always on your side.)

16:31.979 --> 16:33.149
(I love you, Eclipse. I can't live without you guys.)

16:35.649 --> 16:37.279
(I love you, Ryu Sun Jae.)

16:59.509 --> 17:01.170
- Sol!
- Hey!

17:02.139 --> 17:04.039
- Sol!
- You're here.

17:04.040 --> 17:06.450
- Have you been well?
- Yes. You're here early.

17:17.720 --> 17:20.430
(I'm always grateful.)

17:30.899 --> 17:32.739
Then what should we eat?

17:32.740 --> 17:34.339
- Tteokbokki?
- Sounds good.

17:34.340 --> 17:36.178
It took five years for them to hold a concert because of somebody.

17:36.179 --> 17:38.039
It's not like this is Ryu Sun Jae's solo concert.

17:38.040 --> 17:40.349
Seriously. In Hyuk isn't some filler on stage.

17:40.350 --> 17:42.050
If he wants to be an actor, he can just leave the band.

17:42.449 --> 17:44.049
What does he think he's doing?

17:44.050 --> 17:45.279
Is he trying to use Eclipse as his crutch?

17:45.280 --> 17:46.789
Fans like them are the origin...

17:46.790 --> 17:48.188
of breakup rumors surrounding the band.

17:48.189 --> 17:49.219
Exactly.

17:49.260 --> 17:51.719
Our kind Sun Jae still considers people like them his fans.

17:51.760 --> 17:53.628
So even when they write hate comments and spread rumors,

17:53.629 --> 17:55.260
he's letting that slide. Seriously.

17:59.899 --> 18:01.000
Wait.

18:04.899 --> 18:05.908
Hello?

18:05.909 --> 18:09.169
Hello. This is Choi Jung Hoon. I'm calling from Bon Cinema.

18:09.310 --> 18:10.809
You applied for an internship, correct?

18:10.810 --> 18:12.340
I'm calling you after checking your portfolio.

18:13.010 --> 18:14.479
Yes! I did apply for it!

18:14.480 --> 18:15.809
By the way, is it possible...

18:15.810 --> 18:17.649
to come in for an interview now?

18:18.179 --> 18:19.289
Now?

18:19.290 --> 18:21.449
We need to process this really urgently.

18:21.949 --> 18:22.989
If you can't...

18:22.990 --> 18:24.418
I'll be there. I can!

18:24.419 --> 18:25.619
Thank you.

18:27.290 --> 18:28.590
Are you going somewhere?

18:28.629 --> 18:30.029
We have two hours left until we can enter.

18:30.030 --> 18:31.259
Yes, it's an interview for an internship.

18:31.260 --> 18:33.428
I'll be back in a jiffy. Get in line first. Okay?

18:33.429 --> 18:34.770
- Don't be late. Okay?
- Okay.

18:55.820 --> 18:56.820
You're all set.

19:20.409 --> 19:21.948
(Planning Room, Editing Room)

19:21.949 --> 19:23.319
I think it looks good.

19:23.320 --> 19:24.480
That's fine.

19:28.919 --> 19:29.959
Get back to work.

19:30.659 --> 19:32.629
What brings you here?

19:33.959 --> 19:34.989
I got a phone call just now.

19:34.990 --> 19:36.600
I'm here for the internship interview.

19:36.800 --> 19:37.929
I see.

19:41.000 --> 19:42.740
I see.

19:45.899 --> 19:47.809
I would love to work with you,

19:47.810 --> 19:49.908
but as you can see, this is a two-story building...

19:49.909 --> 19:51.340
without an elevator.

19:52.280 --> 19:53.649
- I'm truly sorry.
- Darn it.

19:53.780 --> 19:55.050
What a bummer!

19:55.580 --> 19:56.979
I would have gotten the job...

19:56.980 --> 19:58.379
if it weren't for those annoying stairs.

20:03.119 --> 20:05.119
Why don't I go and see Sun Jae perform?

20:17.969 --> 20:19.269
Why aren't you back already?

20:19.270 --> 20:20.810
We'll enter pretty soon.

20:37.020 --> 20:39.260
Excuse me!

20:40.590 --> 20:41.829
I'm really sorry.

20:41.830 --> 20:43.659
Could you please let me in?

20:43.760 --> 20:45.128
Were you not able to go in?

20:45.129 --> 20:46.729
I really wanted to get here quickly.

20:46.730 --> 20:48.698
You can't enter past the admission time.

20:48.699 --> 20:50.570
I know that. I'm well aware.

20:56.740 --> 20:59.039
It's the last day of the year. So it was so hard to get a cab.

20:59.040 --> 21:00.878
I went through so much trouble of taking the bus...

21:00.879 --> 21:02.480
and barely managed to come here.

21:02.949 --> 21:04.480
But I ended up coming late.

21:05.520 --> 21:08.090
I can tell that you're very good at your job.

21:08.149 --> 21:09.149
Could you please...

21:09.350 --> 21:10.590
help me out?

21:14.629 --> 21:17.060
Well, I really shouldn't.

21:18.459 --> 21:19.629
It's cold.

21:20.000 --> 21:21.169
Gosh, it's so cold.

21:26.510 --> 21:29.138
If you show me your ticket, I'll let you in.

21:29.139 --> 21:31.040
Really? Thank you!

21:31.909 --> 21:32.980
Hold on.

21:36.820 --> 21:37.850
What?

21:41.550 --> 21:42.619
Where did it go?

21:50.760 --> 21:51.800
I'm screwed.

22:03.209 --> 22:04.340
(Let's kidnap Sun Jae and run!)

22:04.810 --> 22:05.980
(Let's kidnap Sun Jae and run!)

22:11.419 --> 22:13.750
(Let's kidnap Sun Jae and run!)

22:15.449 --> 22:18.888
Ryu Sun Jae, Baek In Hyuk, Hyun Su, Jay.

22:18.889 --> 22:20.859
Eclipse!

22:23.500 --> 22:25.128
- Towards the sunset - The sunset!

22:25.129 --> 22:26.830
- Fly with all your strength - Fly

22:27.030 --> 22:28.769
- Bring back the dreams - Bring back the dreams

22:28.770 --> 22:30.500
- That have been forgotten - That have been forgotten

22:30.669 --> 22:32.339
- In the city, there's a chance - Chance!

22:32.340 --> 22:34.108
- If the wall is high, break it - Break it

22:34.109 --> 22:38.009
- Follow your heart - Follow your heart

22:38.010 --> 22:41.208
In the burning sunset, the old days get hot

22:41.209 --> 22:43.549
- The moment we've been waiting for - Waiting for

22:43.550 --> 22:45.049
- Right now - Right now

22:45.050 --> 22:46.918
I've got zero problems

22:46.919 --> 22:50.520
- I'll start running again right now - Running again

22:53.230 --> 22:57.030
Believe me, don't you worry

22:57.159 --> 23:00.869
- We'll meet each other after all - We'll meet each other

23:01.169 --> 23:05.040
You save me like a god of love

23:05.199 --> 23:09.010
We'll meet each other in the end

23:12.639 --> 23:14.080
Remember

23:14.449 --> 23:18.850
You shine so brightly

23:19.750 --> 23:22.990
When you feel like hiding

23:23.320 --> 23:28.330
Like the night sky that embraces us

23:30.659 --> 23:35.330
Every moment of every day, stay with me

23:36.270 --> 23:40.969
- Just you and I, for you and I - Just you and I, for you and I

23:41.310 --> 23:45.679
- You and I, just you and I - You and I, just you and I

23:54.550 --> 23:55.719
This song...

23:56.659 --> 23:58.020
is our debut song.

23:59.520 --> 24:02.590
It's been a long while since I sang it live.

24:04.030 --> 24:05.500
Is Sun Jae talking right now?

24:05.929 --> 24:07.029
What is he saying?

24:07.030 --> 24:08.899
(Let's kidnap Sun Jae and run!)

24:16.609 --> 24:21.879
I didn't want it to stop

24:22.609 --> 24:24.648
- On the day - This song wasn't on the setlist.

24:24.649 --> 24:28.090
You first came to me

24:29.889 --> 24:33.490
I didn't want you to be the rain

24:33.659 --> 24:37.329
That soaks me wet only momentarily

24:37.330 --> 24:41.629
I've prayed so hard

24:43.340 --> 24:45.938
Do you know how I feel?

24:45.939 --> 24:51.408
I've dreamt of you every day

24:51.409 --> 24:55.980
My heart is soaked in you again today

24:57.719 --> 25:01.289
- You are a gift - You are a gift

25:01.290 --> 25:04.589
From the sky

25:04.590 --> 25:07.428
When you're all alone in this world

25:07.429 --> 25:12.359
- I'll protect you - I'll protect you

25:12.629 --> 25:16.899
You have fallen to me

25:17.100 --> 25:20.809
Like a sudden shower

25:20.810 --> 25:22.770
(Let's kidnap Sun Jae and run!)

25:23.139 --> 25:26.709
But I sing to you again today

25:27.179 --> 25:31.219
My precious

25:33.219 --> 25:36.219
Love

25:53.540 --> 25:56.480
Please move carefully and slowly.

25:56.909 --> 25:59.849
Many people are heading home.

25:59.850 --> 26:03.218
Please head to the bus stops nearby.

26:03.219 --> 26:04.719
(We've got your hunger covered!)

26:05.820 --> 26:08.050
It was so touching, though I heard it from outside.

26:08.649 --> 26:10.619
If I had seen it myself, I would have passed out.

26:14.659 --> 26:15.990
This is the first snow of the season.

26:19.260 --> 26:20.600
Sun Jae must be thrilled.

26:22.830 --> 26:23.869
Let's go home now!

26:40.550 --> 26:43.459
What a day today!

26:53.270 --> 26:55.230
In Hyuk, calm down, please.

27:00.209 --> 27:01.909
- In Hyuk, let it go.
- Move!

27:03.010 --> 27:04.639
- You!
- In Hyuk!

27:04.810 --> 27:07.009
- Who do you think I am?
- You should talk it out.

27:07.010 --> 27:08.510
- Let go of me!
- Talk it out.

27:09.250 --> 27:10.320
In Hyuk.

27:13.090 --> 27:15.389
How could you let me find out about your retirement from someone else?

27:16.050 --> 27:17.060
You're retiring?

27:17.320 --> 27:19.889
- Are you out of your mind?
- In Hyuk.

27:21.760 --> 27:22.830
Let's do this some other time.

27:23.659 --> 27:25.830
I'd like to be alone for a moment.

27:29.270 --> 27:31.270
Sure. Do as you please.

27:34.010 --> 27:36.209
Don't do this!

27:36.679 --> 27:37.709
In Hyuk!

28:07.570 --> 28:09.840
Why is the bus stop so far away?

28:10.709 --> 28:13.179
And why is this bridge so long?

28:16.520 --> 28:18.350
Wait. What?

28:19.080 --> 28:20.750
You can't stop right here.

28:22.949 --> 28:23.959
There you go.

28:24.159 --> 28:26.359
Let's go a little further, please.

28:27.330 --> 28:28.359
What?

28:30.359 --> 28:31.429
Gosh.

28:32.300 --> 28:33.570
Are you serious?

28:39.240 --> 28:41.240
I would love to work with you,

28:41.469 --> 28:43.579
but as you can see, this is a two-story building...

28:43.580 --> 28:44.840
without an elevator.

28:45.080 --> 28:47.649
If you show me your ticket, I'll let you in.

29:05.100 --> 29:06.100
It's so cold.

30:26.580 --> 30:27.709
What are you doing right here?

30:29.580 --> 30:30.679
Did your wheelchair...

30:31.649 --> 30:32.719
break down?

30:32.980 --> 30:33.990
What?

30:35.050 --> 30:36.149
Right. Yes.

30:36.520 --> 30:38.789
Dear mouth, say something.

30:38.790 --> 30:41.730
It's Sun Jae. Why aren't you saying anything?

30:59.540 --> 31:00.609
You looked cold.

31:09.990 --> 31:11.619
Thank you.

31:15.060 --> 31:16.159
Why are you crying, then?

31:17.060 --> 31:18.159
I didn't make you cry.

31:19.459 --> 31:20.469
I'm crying...

31:21.169 --> 31:22.399
because I'm so happy.

31:24.939 --> 31:26.399
Actually, I...

31:26.740 --> 31:29.639
I'm your fan.

31:30.510 --> 31:31.540
I can tell.

31:33.510 --> 31:36.780
(Let's kidnap Sun Jae and run!)

31:38.080 --> 31:39.080
Right.

31:43.590 --> 31:44.590
This is funny.

31:45.459 --> 31:46.459
It's a nickname I've been using on the fan club website...

31:46.460 --> 31:47.659
for more than ten years.

31:48.760 --> 31:51.729
Actually, I've been your fan since your debut.

31:51.730 --> 31:52.959
I haven't been distracted by other singers, not even once.

31:53.530 --> 31:54.600
Thank you.

31:55.899 --> 31:57.240
I'm the one who should thank you.

31:58.040 --> 31:59.040
What?

32:02.010 --> 32:03.909
For giving me the will the live again.

32:07.379 --> 32:10.149
I want to thank you for everything.

32:10.649 --> 32:12.379
For existing in this world.

32:13.649 --> 32:15.520
All fans feel the same way.

32:19.060 --> 32:20.230
How are you getting home?

32:20.760 --> 32:22.830
- Well...
- Do you want me to ride you home?

32:24.330 --> 32:26.429
- What?
- I can't leave you behind...

32:26.770 --> 32:28.030
when you're my fan.

32:38.439 --> 32:40.850
My friend is here to pick me up.

32:50.560 --> 32:53.119
Thank you for everything today.

33:02.100 --> 33:03.270
Take it with you.

33:10.070 --> 33:11.879
Give me a second.

33:13.409 --> 33:14.980
It's unfortunate I have nothing to give you.

33:16.149 --> 33:17.149
But...

33:17.750 --> 33:19.719
I know you like these.

33:21.590 --> 33:22.719
Will you take these?

33:37.500 --> 33:40.939
Mom, the one who saved me when I had the accident...

33:41.469 --> 33:43.169
Do you remember his or her name?

33:44.740 --> 33:45.840
No.

33:46.310 --> 33:48.209
That's so long ago.

33:49.280 --> 33:50.519
Why do you ask all of a sudden?

33:50.520 --> 33:53.349
It's nothing. Because I met the person who made me live,

33:53.350 --> 33:54.750
I wondered about the person who saved me.

33:55.250 --> 33:57.260
I feel bad because I didn't thank the person back then.

34:25.879 --> 34:26.920
Right.

34:29.449 --> 34:31.589
I should have gotten this autographed.

34:36.429 --> 34:38.460
It feels like I just woke from a dream.

34:48.610 --> 34:50.810
Wait. What was it?

34:55.210 --> 34:56.610
Did I see it wrong?

35:09.659 --> 35:12.400
Will Sun Jae's wrist be this big?

35:12.560 --> 35:13.569
About this big?

35:25.710 --> 35:28.949
What's up with the outfit today?

35:31.480 --> 35:32.520
Gosh.

35:32.920 --> 35:34.920
My Sun Jae looks better in person.

35:35.190 --> 35:37.290
The camera can't deliver his beauty.

35:38.159 --> 35:41.529
Goodness. This is crazy!

35:44.659 --> 35:45.799
I'm not the guilty one here.

35:46.330 --> 35:47.630
This collarbone is the guilty one.

35:48.029 --> 35:51.369
Gosh. Look at this.

35:54.339 --> 35:58.379
(Mr. Kim)

35:58.380 --> 36:00.138
(Mr. Kim)

36:00.139 --> 36:03.850
(Mr. Kim, Missed calls)

36:42.949 --> 36:45.159
Hey. I ran into Ryu Sun Jae in the lobby.

36:45.319 --> 36:47.258
Really? I'm jealous.

36:47.259 --> 36:48.630
How was he? Was he tall? What about his shoulders?

36:48.730 --> 36:49.758
Is he handsome?

36:49.759 --> 36:50.928
His face is that of CG.

36:50.929 --> 36:53.259
Hey. How come you saw him alone? I wish I had seen him too.

36:59.600 --> 37:02.469
(Let's kidnap Sun Jae and run! Group Chat)

37:03.409 --> 37:06.110
(A new message has arrived.)

37:16.089 --> 37:17.089
(Did you see the news?)

37:17.090 --> 37:18.588
- Did you see the article?
- What's up with that article?

37:18.589 --> 37:19.859
Come on. We've been through this many times.

37:19.860 --> 37:21.829
- What if it's true?
- I don't believe it.

37:21.830 --> 37:23.588
The reporters are giving a false report again.

37:23.589 --> 37:25.060
Does it even make sense that he tried to kill himself?

37:25.759 --> 37:27.100
What are they talking about?

37:28.600 --> 37:30.969
He was right before my eyes not so long ago. How could he...

37:32.839 --> 37:35.909
It must be the haters spreading a rumor again.

37:36.639 --> 37:37.880
(Let's kidnap Sun Jae and run! Group Chat)

37:39.580 --> 37:40.810
(Breaking news, Singer Ryu Sun Jae is reported dead.)

37:42.150 --> 37:43.480
(The report is being checked.)

37:46.380 --> 37:47.420
(There are video clips too!)

37:53.489 --> 37:54.529
My goodness!

37:54.989 --> 37:56.189
That's Ryu Sun Jae, right?

37:56.190 --> 37:57.758
- Yes.
- Oh, no!

37:57.759 --> 37:59.730
I don't think he's breathing.

38:01.029 --> 38:02.100
Oh, no!

38:04.440 --> 38:07.040
No way. Was it Sun Jae? It can't be, can it?

38:08.310 --> 38:09.409
No way.

38:10.369 --> 38:11.440
- Is he going to be all right?
- Oh, no.

38:13.880 --> 38:14.880
(- The concert has just finished. - Isn't it a fake news?)

38:14.880 --> 38:15.880
(- Haters are on it again. - This is a false report, right?)

38:16.049 --> 38:17.519
He's being transferred to Hanguk University Hospital.

38:17.520 --> 38:19.779
Hanguk University Hospital?

38:39.069 --> 38:41.239
Clear the way. We have an emergency patient!

39:00.529 --> 39:01.589
My goodness!

39:26.520 --> 39:27.589
Shock!

39:28.250 --> 39:30.049
- Charge 150 joules.
- Charging 150 joules.

39:41.469 --> 39:42.469
Charging complete.

39:42.770 --> 39:43.770
Shock!

39:52.210 --> 39:53.210
Charge 200 joules.

39:53.710 --> 39:54.710
Shock!

40:04.389 --> 40:06.819
At 12am on January 1st, 2023.

40:07.330 --> 40:10.290
Patient Ryu Sun Jae has passed away.

40:18.139 --> 40:19.770
(The unfortunate passing of Ryu Sun Jae from Eclipse)

40:21.839 --> 40:22.908
(Breaking news)

40:22.909 --> 40:23.980
(The unfortunate passing of Ryu Sun Jae from Eclipse)

40:24.810 --> 40:25.880
Sun Jae.

40:27.250 --> 40:29.850
No. It can't be right.

40:30.750 --> 40:31.779
No.

40:35.089 --> 40:36.089
(Ryu Sun Jae)

40:36.090 --> 40:37.419
(Ryu Sun Jae, Profile)

40:37.420 --> 40:38.888
(Ryu Sun Jae was about to announce his retirement.)

40:38.889 --> 40:40.119
(Ryu Sun Jae suffered from depression...)

40:42.960 --> 40:44.960
(and anxiety and was under medication.)

40:48.330 --> 40:49.429
You looked cold.

40:49.969 --> 40:52.399
No. This isn't true.

40:52.400 --> 40:54.170
You were alive a moment ago.

40:55.770 --> 40:57.779
(Ryu Sun Jae is assumed to have committed suicide.)

40:58.779 --> 40:59.839
Thank you...

41:00.880 --> 41:01.980
for staying alive.

41:05.920 --> 41:07.020
Sun Jae.

41:08.350 --> 41:10.319
You should live your life today...

41:10.790 --> 41:12.060
because it's a great day.

41:13.460 --> 41:15.029
It even snowed today.

41:15.929 --> 41:18.159
You like a snowy day.

41:19.500 --> 41:22.529
Why didn't you continue to live your life today?

41:56.730 --> 41:57.770
Sol.

41:58.339 --> 42:00.868
You're dozing off, aren't you?

42:00.869 --> 42:04.079
What kind of dream did you have that made you mourn bitterly?

42:04.080 --> 42:05.080
Bulldog?

42:05.480 --> 42:06.480
"Bulldog?"

42:09.980 --> 42:11.150
For goodness' sake.

42:11.380 --> 42:12.419
Am I in a classroom?

42:12.420 --> 42:13.749
Yes, you're in a classroom.

42:13.750 --> 42:15.089
It can't be your master bedroom, can it?

42:15.290 --> 42:17.488
You're still dreaming, aren't you?

42:17.489 --> 42:19.690
Right. Is this a dream?

42:19.790 --> 42:20.929
"Is this a dream?"

42:21.230 --> 42:22.330
Look at you.

42:22.560 --> 42:24.600
Stand up at once!

42:24.900 --> 42:26.830
One, two, three!

42:28.429 --> 42:31.069
Gosh. Stand behind the classroom until you're fully awake.

42:32.069 --> 42:34.610
Okay. Where were we? Page 64?

42:34.739 --> 42:36.739
Open page 64...

42:37.509 --> 42:38.580
What are you doing?

42:43.350 --> 42:44.650
Is this really a dream?

42:46.549 --> 42:47.619
Does that mean...

42:49.920 --> 42:50.960
It's Jagam High School!

42:55.659 --> 42:56.690
Im Sol!

42:56.790 --> 42:57.900
Where are you going?

42:58.299 --> 42:59.600
Im Sol!

43:10.040 --> 43:11.210
Where is Sun Jae?

43:11.639 --> 43:12.739
What?

43:12.940 --> 43:14.449
Where is Sun Jae?

43:14.679 --> 43:17.520
(Galhyun Indoor Swimming Pool)

43:20.520 --> 43:23.149
Park Tae Hwan's mock competition...

43:23.150 --> 43:24.388
- at 2008 Beijing Summer Olympics...
- Please check it.

43:24.389 --> 43:26.119
will begin in a moment.

43:27.060 --> 43:28.290
Now.

43:30.029 --> 43:33.130
Athletes, please proceed to the arena now.

43:50.650 --> 43:53.080
(2008 Beijing Olympics Mock Competition Training)

44:14.969 --> 44:17.339
One, two,

44:17.909 --> 44:20.080
three, four.

44:20.139 --> 44:22.449
The weather is amazing today.

44:22.679 --> 44:24.949
It seems like a sign of a dazzling summer.

44:26.420 --> 44:29.089
Singer Bob Marley said something like this.

44:29.250 --> 44:30.988
"The Sun is shining."

44:30.989 --> 44:32.489
"The weather is sweet."

44:32.719 --> 44:34.989
"It makes you want to move your dancing feet."

44:37.799 --> 44:39.429
It's a dazzling day...

44:39.460 --> 44:41.999
that makes your heart pound,

44:42.000 --> 44:43.699
reminding you of someone you cherish.

44:46.969 --> 44:49.509
Even if just one second passes, the present becomes the past.

44:50.009 --> 44:52.409
The most special moment in your life...

44:52.739 --> 44:56.279
would be today where you stay with your loved one.

44:56.710 --> 44:59.179
Before it's too late,

44:59.549 --> 45:01.819
run to your loved one right now.

46:56.799 --> 46:58.170
Sun Jae!

47:16.949 --> 47:17.960
Who is it?

47:18.219 --> 47:19.259
Get out!

47:44.679 --> 47:45.779
What are you doing?

47:51.960 --> 47:55.290
You must've been struggling by yourself, feeling so lonely.

47:55.589 --> 47:58.100
You couldn't even tell anyone that you were having a hard time.

47:58.630 --> 48:00.630
I didn't know you were in so much pain.

48:01.330 --> 48:02.869
I'm sorry I didn't notice it.

48:07.770 --> 48:09.139
I love you, Sun Jae.

48:15.810 --> 48:17.149
Did you not see the "no entrance" sign?

48:17.150 --> 48:19.218
- Drag her out!
- Why?

48:19.219 --> 48:21.020
It's a dream. Let me just stay with him.

48:21.049 --> 48:22.250
Sun Jae.

48:22.290 --> 48:24.489
I love you, Sun Jae!

48:24.790 --> 48:26.520
Sun Jae!

48:26.589 --> 48:28.589
Let go of me!

48:28.790 --> 48:30.389
Sun Jae!

48:32.659 --> 48:34.199
Wait. Let go of me.

48:34.259 --> 48:36.500
Give me a moment.

48:36.630 --> 48:37.940
Let me go inside just for a moment.

48:38.239 --> 48:39.269
No.

48:39.270 --> 48:41.468
This game is being conducted in strict secrecy.

48:41.469 --> 48:42.809
Don't you ever talk about it to someone else.

48:42.810 --> 48:44.068
Let me go inside just once.

48:44.069 --> 48:45.540
If you understand, you should leave right now.

48:46.480 --> 48:48.909
Are you all right?

48:49.909 --> 48:51.520
No, it hurts.

48:54.989 --> 48:56.089
It hurts?

48:56.819 --> 48:57.889
Why?

49:02.190 --> 49:03.659
Why can I not wake up from the dream?

49:04.330 --> 49:06.759
I was definitely looking for Sun Jae's watch.

49:13.270 --> 49:14.369
I found it.

49:14.710 --> 49:16.069
And...

49:16.540 --> 49:17.880
then...

49:22.750 --> 49:23.880
No way.

49:27.719 --> 49:29.650
Your body will remain,

49:29.850 --> 49:31.388
but your spirit will leave this world...

49:31.389 --> 49:33.659
when you have fulfilled the time in this world.

49:33.920 --> 49:38.060
Your spirit crosses long Sanzu Bridge...

49:38.130 --> 49:40.029
to go to the underworld.

49:41.029 --> 49:42.270
Am I...

49:42.770 --> 49:43.969
dead?

49:59.679 --> 50:00.719
Hey.

50:05.360 --> 50:07.290
Hey, what are you doing?

50:12.600 --> 50:13.659
Hey.

50:14.600 --> 50:15.630
I'm sorry.

50:16.799 --> 50:18.770
We're dead, right?

50:20.670 --> 50:21.710
What?

50:26.409 --> 50:27.509
Are you a ghost?

50:28.210 --> 50:29.279
"A ghost?"

50:34.750 --> 50:35.819
You're Sun Jae.

50:39.489 --> 50:40.689
Hey, why are you crying?

50:40.690 --> 50:43.259
Right. I can see him.

50:43.730 --> 50:45.360
It means I'm dead.

50:48.469 --> 50:49.600
What is wrong with her?

50:50.869 --> 50:51.999
Here.

50:52.000 --> 50:53.039
I have the same watch.

50:53.040 --> 50:54.540
It's yours. Take it.

50:55.210 --> 50:56.670
- It's mine?
- Yes.

50:56.770 --> 50:58.139
This is actually better.

50:59.339 --> 51:00.439
I'll go with you.

51:00.440 --> 51:02.909
I'll go with you so that you don't feel lonely on the way there.

51:05.980 --> 51:08.690
But what about my poor mom?

51:08.949 --> 51:12.819
Mom. Grandma.

51:13.190 --> 51:14.190
No.

51:14.191 --> 51:16.290
I haven't crossed the bridge yet. There must be a way.

51:17.790 --> 51:19.000
Let's go back together.

51:19.360 --> 51:21.270
Never cross this bridge.

51:21.429 --> 51:23.000
I should if I want to go home.

51:23.969 --> 51:25.000
No.

51:25.900 --> 51:27.738
No, Sun Jae. You shouldn't cross the bridge.

51:27.739 --> 51:29.409
Yes, I should.

51:30.909 --> 51:32.210
No, Sun Jae.

51:33.639 --> 51:35.380
Let's live together. Okay?

51:35.480 --> 51:37.210
Let's live together.

51:38.650 --> 51:39.819
"Let's live together?"

51:41.420 --> 51:42.488
Taxi!

51:42.489 --> 51:43.750
- Sun Jae!
- Taxi!

51:46.060 --> 51:47.159
Please go straight.

51:47.190 --> 51:48.330
Sun Jae!

51:52.429 --> 51:53.560
There's a cab...

51:54.400 --> 51:55.500
in the underworld?

52:03.270 --> 52:04.610
(Mom)

52:09.049 --> 52:10.109
Hello?

52:10.110 --> 52:11.250
Where are you?

52:11.350 --> 52:12.920
I heard you had skipped school!

52:13.650 --> 52:15.019
It's really Mom's voice.

52:15.020 --> 52:16.588
Cut the chatter and come home quickly.

52:16.589 --> 52:17.888
If you don't come back in an hour,

52:17.889 --> 52:20.520
you're going to take an express train to the underworld!

52:21.989 --> 52:23.130
The underworld?

52:27.630 --> 52:28.630
(Training Journal)

52:31.799 --> 52:32.869
(Tests in Exercise Science)

52:36.440 --> 52:39.279
Oh, my. Sun Jae, the Shortfin Mako.

52:39.339 --> 52:42.008
What's "Shortfin Mako?" It's weird.

52:42.009 --> 52:44.778
Hey. Jo O Ryeon, the Asian Seal.

52:44.779 --> 52:46.079
Park Tae Hwan, the Marine Boy.

52:46.080 --> 52:48.150
You need a nickname too.

52:49.190 --> 52:51.250
How did the game go today?

52:51.360 --> 52:52.619
It wasn't even an official competition.

52:53.489 --> 52:54.520
But...

52:54.929 --> 52:55.988
the records were good.

52:55.989 --> 52:58.299
I knew it. I'm proud of you, son.

52:58.330 --> 53:00.460
I knew you would make it.

53:01.159 --> 53:02.500
How was your shoulder?

53:02.600 --> 53:03.869
Of course, it was fine.

53:08.170 --> 53:10.069
Father, I'm going to eat.

53:11.210 --> 53:12.710
Yes. See you later.

53:21.420 --> 53:24.520
You must've been struggling by yourself, feeling so lonely.

53:25.060 --> 53:27.460
You couldn't even tell anyone that you were having a hard time.

53:27.960 --> 53:29.929
I didn't know you were in so much pain.

53:30.659 --> 53:32.230
I'm sorry I didn't notice it.

53:32.929 --> 53:34.259
I love you, Sun Jae.

53:37.069 --> 53:38.339
She wasn't in her right mind.

53:42.310 --> 53:43.339
What?

53:46.710 --> 53:48.779
What? Mine was here.

53:50.449 --> 53:52.480
Why did she give this to me then?

53:57.690 --> 53:58.790
(Gold Videos and DVDs)

53:59.989 --> 54:01.020
(To Let)

54:01.830 --> 54:02.989
(34-1, Nuri-dong)

54:05.330 --> 54:06.330
No way.

54:07.330 --> 54:08.730
It looks just like it did in the past.

54:09.500 --> 54:11.540
The whole area was redeveloped.

54:18.509 --> 54:21.310
Go back to your position as if you didn't attack.

54:22.850 --> 54:23.850
Mom?

54:25.750 --> 54:27.719
Come here.

54:29.850 --> 54:33.019
Hey. Where did you go...

54:33.020 --> 54:34.589
after leaving your bag at school?

54:36.190 --> 54:37.190
Mom.

54:37.759 --> 54:39.028
Why do you look so young?

54:39.029 --> 54:41.868
The flattery is useless, you punk.

54:41.869 --> 54:43.999
Why did you skip school? Where did you go?

54:44.000 --> 54:45.000
You're a senior in high school now.

54:45.001 --> 54:46.399
Why did you do something you've never done before?

54:46.400 --> 54:48.639
- Wait. Hold on.
- My goodness.

54:52.839 --> 54:54.580
"Year 2008?"

54:58.420 --> 55:01.888
My granddaughter surely has good luck when it comes to food.

55:01.889 --> 55:03.920
Come in. Drink the misugaru.

55:04.119 --> 55:05.560
Grandma.

55:05.819 --> 55:08.829
Oh, my. Don't run.

55:08.830 --> 55:10.560
You'll become hungry.

55:11.529 --> 55:12.699
Grandma, look at me.

55:13.330 --> 55:14.499
Who am I?

55:14.500 --> 55:16.929
Why do you ask? You're Sol, my youngest grandchild.

55:20.369 --> 55:22.770
Right. I'm Sol.

55:22.909 --> 55:23.940
My gosh.

55:26.040 --> 55:27.040
Call me again.

55:27.041 --> 55:29.880
Say my name again.

55:30.310 --> 55:31.580
Sol.

55:34.580 --> 55:36.750
Why are you crying?

55:36.850 --> 55:38.790
Who made you cry?

55:40.219 --> 55:41.290
Grandma.

55:42.630 --> 55:43.630
Oh, my.

55:44.960 --> 55:45.960
There, there.

56:08.119 --> 56:09.889
(Im Sol)

56:40.350 --> 56:41.520
If it's June,

56:42.619 --> 56:44.420
it's before the accident happened.

57:04.469 --> 57:05.739
Mom.

57:07.040 --> 57:08.449
Grandma.

57:08.850 --> 57:09.909
Yes.

57:10.850 --> 57:11.949
Why are you crying?

57:16.619 --> 57:18.360
It's weird.

57:19.489 --> 57:22.259
I can't feel my legs.

57:23.790 --> 57:25.199
What happened to me?

57:27.299 --> 57:28.600
I can't remember.

58:18.380 --> 58:21.989
Will I open my eyes here tomorrow?

58:37.469 --> 58:39.339
What if everything disappears like an illusion...

58:40.239 --> 58:42.209
when I wake up...

58:42.210 --> 58:44.270
as if it's a dream on a midsummer night?

59:10.969 --> 59:12.270
I can't move my legs.

59:13.799 --> 59:15.210
I knew it.

59:15.670 --> 59:16.839
It was a dream.

59:22.380 --> 59:23.380
Hey!

59:25.880 --> 59:26.880
What?

59:30.889 --> 59:31.960
What's going on?

59:35.089 --> 59:36.230
Geum.

59:37.159 --> 59:38.730
Im Geum.

59:39.230 --> 59:41.400
My brother!

59:41.500 --> 59:42.900
I'm sorry.

59:46.770 --> 59:48.409
I'm going to school!

59:57.679 --> 01:00:00.980
Make sure to bring a small umbrella when you go out today.

01:00:01.150 --> 01:00:02.689
As the atmosphere becomes unstable,

01:00:02.690 --> 01:00:05.119
rain is forecasted to occur in many places.

01:00:05.360 --> 01:00:07.189
Especially in the Seoul and Gyeonggi Province areas,

01:00:07.190 --> 01:00:10.028
brief showers are expected to form due to the intense heat,

01:00:10.029 --> 01:00:12.630
providing temporary relief from the heat.

01:00:12.860 --> 01:00:14.798
The light showers are expected...

01:00:14.799 --> 01:00:17.199
during the morning.

01:00:21.469 --> 01:00:23.670
No, I don't want to.

01:00:23.839 --> 01:00:25.609
Okay. Let's run.

01:00:25.610 --> 01:00:27.210
Run? I really don't want to.

01:00:28.310 --> 01:00:29.750
I should return it to her.

01:00:38.960 --> 01:00:40.989
Wait for me.

01:00:41.089 --> 01:00:42.159
We should go out.

01:00:42.290 --> 01:00:44.489
- Hey.
- Don't do it.

01:00:51.330 --> 01:00:53.600
- Yes! It's almost over!
- Hurry up and come.

01:00:58.339 --> 01:00:59.480
Sun Jae.

01:01:03.909 --> 01:01:06.819
(Breaking News)

01:01:07.719 --> 01:01:08.719
Sun.

01:01:11.690 --> 01:01:12.859
How was the mock competition yesterday?

01:01:12.860 --> 01:01:14.359
Get off me.

01:01:14.360 --> 01:01:15.488
So did you do well or not?

01:01:15.489 --> 01:01:16.960
Of course, I did well.

01:02:55.290 --> 01:02:56.690
Why are you crying?

01:03:02.230 --> 01:03:03.330
Why are you crying, then?

01:03:03.429 --> 01:03:04.630
I didn't make you cry.

01:03:20.319 --> 01:03:21.948
(We'd like to thank Park Tae Hwan, Kwon Yu Ri, Han Seung Yeon,)

01:03:21.949 --> 01:03:23.049
(and Lee Su Ji for the special appearance.)

01:03:35.230 --> 01:03:38.130
(Lovely Runner)

01:03:38.369 --> 01:03:40.969
I must get close to someone. What should I do?

01:03:42.040 --> 01:03:43.040
Quit smoking.

01:03:43.210 --> 01:03:44.909
Give up. No.

01:03:45.009 --> 01:03:46.739
Have you ever seen me by any chance?

01:03:46.909 --> 01:03:48.009
Even if I have, I haven't.

01:03:48.540 --> 01:03:49.610
Hi. Oh, my gosh.

01:03:49.949 --> 01:03:51.408
They like Kim Tae Sung.

01:03:51.409 --> 01:03:53.318
- Who is Kim Tae Sung?
- You don't know him?

01:03:53.319 --> 01:03:54.980
- You're Ryu Sun Jae, right?
- Who are you?

01:03:55.489 --> 01:03:57.589
Sun Jae, you shouldn't participate in the upcoming competition.

01:04:00.819 --> 01:04:01.860
Who are you?

01:04:02.360 --> 01:04:03.888
Why on earth are you doing this to me?

01:04:03.889 --> 01:04:05.130
Because I want to protect you.

01:04:05.429 --> 01:04:07.529
I'm trying anything because I have to save you.

01:04:09.494 --> 01:04:11.494
Dramaday.me
